WEBVTT

00:00:08,940 --> 00:00:13,260
We look forward to your testimony in opposition to the legislation.

00:00:13,260 --> 00:00:15,660
If five minutes, ma'am, please proceed.

00:00:15,660 --> 00:00:18,620
Committee members, thank you very much for the opportunity to speak.

00:00:18,620 --> 00:00:21,100
I'm Sharon Goldberg. I'm an internal medicine physician.

00:00:21,100 --> 00:00:26,300
I've practiced medicine for 21 years, and my background is mostly academic internal medicine,

00:00:26,300 --> 00:00:29,660
hospital-based, clinical research, and medical education.

00:00:31,260 --> 00:00:36,700
I am going to skip many of the things I wanted to say because I didn't realize it was only five minutes.

00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:41,020
Wireless radiation has biological effects, period.

00:00:42,380 --> 00:00:46,940
This is no longer a subject for debate when you look at pub med and the peer review literature.

00:00:47,660 --> 00:00:53,340
These effects are seen in all life forms, plants, animals, insects, microbes.

00:00:54,220 --> 00:00:58,300
In humans, we have clear evidence of cancer now. There is no question.

00:00:59,340 --> 00:01:05,020
We have evidence of DNA damage, cardiomyopathy, which is the precursor of congestive heart failure.

00:01:05,900 --> 00:01:12,460
Neuropsychiatric effects. 5G is not a conversation about whether or not these biological effects

00:01:12,460 --> 00:01:19,660
exist. They clearly do. 5G is a conversation about unsustainable healthcare expenditures.

00:01:20,220 --> 00:01:26,860
Why do I say this? We've been sitting on the evidence for EMR and chronic disease for decades.

00:01:28,060 --> 00:01:31,340
And now, we are seeing all these epidemics appearing.

00:01:32,060 --> 00:01:36,220
So, diabetes is the first epidemic. I think most of you know the statistics.

00:01:36,220 --> 00:01:41,500
They're very scary. One in three American children will become diabetic in their lifetime,

00:01:41,500 --> 00:01:44,540
and if they're Hispanic females, the number is one in two.

00:01:45,980 --> 00:01:51,100
So, what does this have to do with wireless radiation? Wireless radiation and other electromagnetic

00:01:51,100 --> 00:01:56,620
fields, such as magnetic fields and dirty electricity, have been clearly associated with elevated

00:01:56,620 --> 00:02:02,140
blood sugar and diabetes. That is what the peer-reviewed literature says. It is not opinion.

00:02:02,780 --> 00:02:10,460
The closer you live to a cell tower, the higher your blood glucose that is based on hemoglobin A1C

00:02:10,460 --> 00:02:16,140
measurements. So, the idea with small cells of putting the cells closer to people's homes and

00:02:16,140 --> 00:02:21,980
bedrooms scientifically is very dangerous, and from an economic perspective, it's dangerous.

00:02:21,980 --> 00:02:27,020
And you may not know this. I was shocked to find this out, but the way you create a model

00:02:27,020 --> 00:02:34,700
of diabetes in rats in the lab is by exposing them to 2.4 gigahertz, and this is not for long-term

00:02:34,700 --> 00:02:42,700
exposure. So, I don't have time to talk about the costs, but the huge problem with diabetes really

00:02:42,700 --> 00:02:51,660
is chronic kidney disease. End-stage renal disease, the worst complication of diabetes, leads

00:02:51,660 --> 00:02:58,700
to hemodialysis. Hemodialysis is an automatic qualification for Medicare, and if you don't qualify

00:02:58,700 --> 00:03:06,780
for Medicare, we still have to dialize the patient, and the state ends up paying in many different

00:03:06,780 --> 00:03:15,900
instances. So, renal failure is 1% of Medicare, but it takes up 7% of all Medicare expenditures.

00:03:16,860 --> 00:03:22,940
I don't have time to talk about this anymore, but once again, we have, so the other epidemics

00:03:22,940 --> 00:03:29,100
that clearly link from the science with electromagnetic radiation are related to mental health,

00:03:29,100 --> 00:03:35,340
and this is straight from PubMed. This isn't my opinion, this is science, okay?

00:03:35,340 --> 00:03:39,420
Those of us who aren't physicians, what is PubMed?

00:03:39,420 --> 00:03:45,740
I'm sorry. It's just the, it's our National Library of Medicine. This is where you would go,

00:03:45,740 --> 00:03:51,900
this is just the peer reviewed literature. So, we have three epidemics that clearly, they're

00:03:51,900 --> 00:03:57,980
essentially one epidemic. We have deterioration of mental health in the United States, and if you look,

00:03:58,620 --> 00:04:03,900
really at the science, what does it show? So, and these epidemics are our suicide epidemic,

00:04:06,220 --> 00:04:12,460
epidemics in violent, so shootings, and the opioid epidemic. And I don't have five minutes

00:04:12,460 --> 00:04:16,780
is not the time to talk about this. This is in the peer reviewed literature. I have a file to

00:04:16,780 --> 00:04:21,580
submit for the record, but these are facts, these aren't, and these are things that have just been

00:04:21,580 --> 00:04:26,300
glossed over by the wireless industry, and I really don't have time to talk about them in five minutes,

00:04:26,300 --> 00:04:33,260
I wish I did. But we need to examine our epidemics in the context of our EMF exposures. What does that

00:04:33,260 --> 00:04:41,820
mean? That means that the CDC tracking these epidemics needs to, we need to start measuring

00:04:41,820 --> 00:04:49,500
how much radiation are people being exposed to, and before we roll out 5G, and this means

00:04:50,300 --> 00:04:55,660
there are four kinds of electromagnetic fields that we know are harmful to human health,

00:04:55,660 --> 00:05:01,980
so radio frequency radiation, magnetic fields, dirty electricity, and electric fields, okay,

00:05:02,540 --> 00:05:09,420
our exposure, any given person, and all humans are affected by EMFs, our given exposure

00:05:10,300 --> 00:05:15,660
has nothing to do with the research that my colleagues are going to cite, with the National

00:05:15,660 --> 00:05:22,140
Toxicology Program. That is an assessment of the risk of one cell phone in the near field, okay.

00:05:23,180 --> 00:05:30,620
What is our exposure? In a day, it's not one cell phone. It's cell phones, it's multiple wireless

00:05:30,620 --> 00:05:37,820
networks, it's smart meters, it's cell towers, it's the sandwich, and it all adds up. And this is a,

00:05:37,820 --> 00:05:44,860
this is a serious problem for occupational health, public safety, and personal safety, and I feel

00:05:44,860 --> 00:05:51,420
that it's irresponsible to be even talking about the internet of things and rolling out a new

00:05:51,420 --> 00:05:58,460
untested technology when we're not even measuring what are our current exposures from the current

00:05:58,460 --> 00:06:00,060
networks.

